The verbatim initial RED is retained in contract-red-contained.log.

Additional test-first bounds found while the CP31 implementation existed:

1. unknown_interface RED
   A syntactically valid compatible-ID function section named interface 200,
   which is not in the active configuration, caused one unnecessary extended-
   properties request. The contract rejected that request. Properties are now
   fetched only when metadata is attached to an actually emitted child.

2. malformed_second_function RED
   A valid MI05 section followed by a malformed second function section leaked
   MI05's partially parsed compatible ID. The contract rejected that partial
   result. Compatible-ID parsing is now atomic: any malformed function section
   clears the entire 256-interface metadata table.

