All 11 scenarios pass against both independent clean builds.

Bounded behavior exercised by the fake backend:
  OS string:       0x80/0x06/0x03ee/0, exactly 18 bytes
  compatible IDs: 0xc0/vendor/0/wIndex 4, 16-byte header then bounded body
  properties:     0xc1/vendor/interface<<8/wIndex 5, 10-byte header then body
  timeout:        1000 ms
  maximum body:   4096 bytes

The request bytes, lengths, order, and absence of extra requests are contract
assertions. Vendor code 0xa5, WINUSB IDs, GUIDs, and malformed blobs are
synthetic fixtures informed by the installed vendor-module model. They are not
evidence that the physical io24 returned those descriptors.
